{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>For you are a stiff-necked people.</b> For it is impossible for there to be justice and uprightness of heart together with stubbornness of the neck. For the stiff-necked man is one who follows the stubbornness of his heart and his own thinking, even though some instructor of righteousness may show him by clear proof that his thinking is bad and leads to harm. This is because he does not turn toward the instructor — as though his neck were a sinew of iron, so that he cannot turn this way or that — but follows the stubbornness of his heart as before."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:20:58.777619553Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}